  "body": "## Summary and dependency\n\nDraft after #374 (`codex/payment-recovery-observability-20260915`), preserving the existing payment stack. Repairs the shared `CheckoutStore` used by Datafast, PayPal, PlaceToPay and PayPhone, plus the existing independently reviewed bank-transfer finalizer. No provider activated, no new payment method, no production deployment or live transaction.\n\nThe initial regressions reproduced **8 failures across all four online providers**: successful capture replay rewrote timestamps; same-amount receipts from another provider/reference were accepted. Inspection also found that resource rebinding could downgrade a successful attempt to processing.\n\n- Validate and lock the exact checkout/attempt pair before binding writes. Reject cross-checkout binding without inserting a resource/audit; permit only monotonic unresolved stage advances. Replayed or terminal bindings preserve payment timestamps/state.\n- Acknowledge an existing capture only when full recorded checkout payment, successful attempt, posted capture ledger and exact receipt identity agree. Return `Right False`, without state/history/receipt updates or new fulfillment transition.\n- Match receipt amount/currency, canonical number, provider and external reference. Retain voided historical receipts; do not reissue them. Reject incomplete or conflicting history instead of silently backfilling it.\n- Permit acknowledgement of the original capture after refund/dispute/chargeback without returning checkout to paid. This does not execute a refund or validate the current refundable balance.\n- Continue rejecting first positive payment on expired/canceled checkouts. No automatic inventory reopening or late-payment accounting policy is invented.\n\n## Verification \u2014 local, 2026-09-15 UTC\n\nFinal runtime source: `03d563c18d7f0ce5339f0e7f0023d55c0c037dc6`; test prerequisite fix: `b2ab560b250fd11ac7c0f3aa98b6dd8f5307ab03`. Initial regression commit: `4a88878d046b36d46361998739fc31fb5951a55a`. Later changes are documentation only.\n\n- `cd tdf-hq && stack test --fast --rerun-tests`: **2,596 examples, 0 failures**, 31.3536 s, exit 0.\n- `sh scripts/test-provider-retry-runtime.sh` against a new private PostgreSQL 16.10 Unix-socket cluster: **170 examples, 0 failures**, 26.5395 s, full harness exit 0 at 15:50:30. Includes all existing 133 cases, 36 online-provider regression cases, and independently approved bank-transfer replay. Existing recovery migration repetition, empty rollback/flag retention and populated rollback refusal/history checks passed.\n- The bank test first failed correctly because its fixture lacked the real canonical bank activation migration. Added that existing disabled-by-default prerequisite, verified bank tests (2 examples), then reran the complete harness on another empty cluster. No production guard was relaxed.\n- A focused command with incorrect `--match` quoting exited before any tests; explicitly not counted as a pass. Initial 141-example red run had the 8 intended regressions; the next 170-example run had only the missing bank fixture failure. Full chronology is retained in the handoff.\n- Web hosted checkout/return regression: **13 tests / 2 suites passed**, 50.557 s.\n- `npm run quality:repo`: passed, **157 Node tests** in nine groups, formal audit and generated-artifact drift guard passed.\n- Catalog gate: **1,422 files / 1,128 candidates, 0 unreviewed / stale**, exit 0. No review entries or gate changes needed. Shell syntax, generated web/mobile byte comparison, local doc links and `git diff --check` passed.\n- All three task-owned test clusters are stopped; exact-path `pg_ctl status` confirmed no server running. Synthetic test data/logs retained for inspection.\n\nAll payment/provider/reviewer evidence is synthetic. Real PostgreSQL is not a merchant sandbox. No actual provider refund, settlement, bank transfer, device test or screenshot was produced. Full native/web source builds were not rerun because those implementations/contracts are unchanged; web regressions and byte-identical generated contracts were checked. Parent #374 backend CI was still pending at 15:48 UTC; no new-PR CI success is claimed.\n\n## Architecture, migration and compatibility\n\nSee `docs/adr/0123-idempotent-capture-evidence-and-binding.md`, `docs/payments/capture-replay-integrity-2026-09-15.md`, and the updated operator runbook for exact commands, sources, observed timestamps and rollback cautions.\n\nNo production SQL migration/manifest/backfill or historical reference rewrite. The disposable harness adds **existing** manual-evidence and canonical bank-account migrations and the minimal ORM party-ID fixture required by their real guards. It is not a complete production-schema rehearsal. No new endpoint: existing authenticated verification routes retain their API shapes and callers' fulfillment responsibilities.\n\nDrain older callback/verification writers before an authorized rollout: old code can still downgrade attempts and mutate historical timestamps. Incomplete legacy receipts now require explicit reconciliation; do not delete/reissue records to force success. A rollback reintroduces these defects, so pause affected consumers and prefer a forward repair.\n\nLatest main `52b32e4c17b3b0485c66e666137f85d44cc962d4` and upstream payment merges #332/#334 were inspected; preserve their separate catalog/test additions when integrating the stack. Mobile remains pinned to draft #81 (`d84fc3196202f2ac2468f78816b3c98fb4a22144`); no new native PR or generated schema change is needed. Its main/#80 divergence remains a coordinated merge dependency.\n\n## Blocked / not done\n\nStaging inspector at 15:18:48.933 found healthy public API/web endpoints but all six hosting checks returned `hosting_authentication_unavailable`; source SHA unknown, providerQualified=false. Restore approved `FLY_STAGING_API_TOKEN` / `FLY_STAGING_WEB_TOKEN` or authorized local Fly login, then qualify exact source/merchant sandbox/webhooks. No secret values were read or printed and no hosting resources were changed.\n\nProvider sandboxes, authenticated staging, late-payment financial quarantine/fulfillment recovery, unknown-resource reconciliation, remaining provider/business flows, compliant seller payouts and legal/accounting/PCI approval remain outstanding. This increment is not whole-platform completion, production readiness or certification. Keep draft and unmerged.\n",
